From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:05:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Every listing's photos copied ahead of visitors, into one
 store for the whole site

The copies now live in R2 (the PHOTOS bucket bound to the site), so a photo copied once is there
for every visitor, wherever Cloudflare serves them; the edge cache in front saves a read, and the
bucket's own rule deletes a copy after 30 days. GET /homes/api/warm, called every minute by the
photo-warmer Worker (Blog-Brain website-patches/photo-warmer-worker.js), takes a page of homes for
sale and copies each first photo not yet kept, in both sizes, at most 12 a call, stopping when the
MLS says fewer than 40 are left this minute or 600 this hour, so visitors still get theirs. It
needs the WARM_KEY secret; without it, or without the bucket, it does nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
